{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":60563,"duration_api_ms":60358,"num_turns":14,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"900e8d79-514b-4628-bd78-a470a786bae5","total_cost_usd":0.35505225000000007,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29229,"cache_read_input_tokens":230912,"output_tokens":2275,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29229,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":2275,"cacheReadInputTokens":230912,"cacheCreationInputTokens":29229,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.35505225000000007,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Accept the two real substrate-model defects (missing microfauna O2 demand and homogenized porosity for layered substrates — noted as duplicates). Reject the micro-optimization accessor complaint and the red-test claim which does not reproduce.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-9df569ce","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified in substrate.rs:127-139: `effective_substrate_porosity` computes a depth-weighted arithmetic mean across all layers. For diffusion through stacked media, this is physically incorrect — a thin low-porosity cap is the rate-limiting barrier and its constraint is diluted by deeper high-porosity layers, producing an overly optimistic D_eff and too-deep oxic boundary. The defect is real and the suggested fix (use topmost-layer porosity or harmonic mean) or a documented TODO is appropriate."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-a9320302","decision":"reject","rationale":"The redundant computation is real but immaterial. Grep confirms the convenience accessors are only called in a test (`substrate.rs:259`), not in any tick-level hot path. The per-call cost is trivial (iterating a small substrate_layers vec). Removing useful test accessors or adding warning comments for a non-problem would be unnecessary churn with no correctness or robustness benefit."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-57228e15","decision":"reject","rationale":"I ran `cargo test -p tank_harness --test e2e_geometry_scaling -- --nocapture` in the current workspace and all 3 tests passed. The file uses `CONCENTRATION_PARITY_TOLERANCE = 0.65` (line 27), not the claimed re-tightened 20%. The amendment describes a failure that does not exist in the submitted code."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-b43b8059","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified in substrate.rs:81-124: `estimate_substrate_o2_demand_rate` sums only decomposer demand and root respiration demand, completely omitting `MicrofaunaState`. The function's own doc comment says it estimates from 'decomposer activity and root respiration', but the bead spec defines substrate O2 demand as including microfauna. The `microfauna` module maintains a population_index and grazing_pressure_index that could contribute substrate-local O2 consumption, especially in detritivore-heavy setups. This is a genuine missing-contributor bug that biases penetration depth too deep."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-0c12a58f","decision":"accept","rationale":"This identifies the same underlying defect as fr-1-9df569ce: the depth-weighted average porosity in substrate.rs:127-139 homogenizes layered substrates in a way that overestimates effective diffusivity when a restrictive layer sits atop a porous one. It is a valid duplicate observation of a real modeling error."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"a5e48b13-db1b-4a3c-a58e-be0870226492"}
